<p id="S2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the horizontal maps glue <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and the
vertical maps forget markings not in <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
In this case, the image of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{A}\circ\iota_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>ι</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{A}\circ\iota_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is a proper boundary divisor in <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,A}</annotation></semantics></math>, which has no holomorphic <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>-forms. Hence, the pullback of the generator of <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{11,0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{11,0}(\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,A})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now suppose <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap B|\geq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap B|\geq 10</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B^{c}\cap A|\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B^{c}\cap A|\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the lower left-hand side of (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 2.2. Generators and their pullbacks ‣ 2. Genus 
        
          1 ‣ The eleventh cohomology group of 
      
        
          
          
            ¯
            M
          
          
            
              
              
              
            
            
              g
              ,
              n" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>) must be replaced by <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,p\cup(B\cap A)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathcal{M}}_{1,p\cup(B\cap A)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, there is another commutative diagram</span></p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

